    {
      "call_source": "transcript_item",
      "params_digest": "8989f1006e204b77",
      "query": "{\"content\": \"Distributed once so far, followed by a Call For Response on February 2, 2026. Expect at least one further distribution once the respondent's brief in opposition is filed, given the Court's affirmative interest. A CVSG is unlikely because the dispute is a private intentional tort (false imprisonment), which lacks the direct federal administrative or sovereign interest that usually prompts a CVSG in bankruptcy cases. \\n\\nIf granted, the Court would likely take QP 1 as written to resol",
